"""L6981x33DR - 38 V 1.5 A synchronous buck converter, fixed 3.3 V output, SO-8. Bare part.

Datasheet: ST DS13554 Rev 3 (December 2022).

Variants (Table 11, p45; same SO-8 pinout and footprint):
- L6981N33DR (default): LNM, low-noise mode. Forced PWM at every load (section 6.4.2,
  p14). The low-side switch sinks inductor current down to IVY_SINK = 1.25 to 1.75 A
  (Table 6, p6; section 6.6.2, p18), so the converter regulates an output that another
  source pulls above the set point by sinking current into VIN.
- L6981C33DR: LCM, low-consumption mode. Pulse skipping below ISKIP = 0.35 A; the low-side
  switch turns off at zero inductor current (section 6.4.1, p10-11). It sinks current only
  in output overvoltage (section 6.6.1, p17).

Pins (Figure 2 and Table 1, p3): 1 SW, 2 BOOT, 3 VCC, 4 VOUT/FB, 5 EN/CLKIN, 6 AGND, 7 VIN,
8 PGND. AGND and PGND are both on GND (PGND to AGND within +-0.3 V, Table 3). VOUT/FB of a
fixed version senses the output through the internal divider and supplies the internal
circuitry (section 6.5, p16). EN/CLKIN is VIN compatible (section 6.1, p9); CLKIN
synchronisation (200 to 500 kHz) exists only on LNM parts (Table 6, p7).

Absolute maximum ratings (Table 3, p5): VIN -0.3 to 42 V; EN -0.3 V to VIN + 0.3 V;
SW -0.85 V to VIN + 0.3 V (-3.9 V for 0.5 ns); VOUT/FB -0.3 to 8 V; VCC -0.3 V to
min(VIN + 0.3 V, 4 V); BOOT SW - 0.3 V to SW + 4 V; high/low-side RMS switch current 1.5 A;
TJ -40 to 150 C.

Operating values (Table 6, p6-7): VIN 3.5 to 38 V; output (VOUT/FB, fixed 3.3 V,
TJ -40 to 125 C) 3.284 / 3.3 / 3.346 V; fSW 360 / 400 / 440 kHz; peak current limit
2.0 to 2.3 A (no slope contribution); valley current limit 1.7 / 2.0 / 2.3 A; EN rising
threshold 1.08 / 1.2 / 1.32 V; VCC LDO 3.0 / 3.3 / 3.6 V; VCC rising (UVLO) threshold 2.3
to 3.3 V; soft-start 1.0 / 1.3 / 1.6 ms after an 800 us typ setup delay (section 6.2, p9);
RDSON high side 0.175 Ohm, low side 0.125 Ohm. RthJA 65 C/W on the ST 2-layer demo board
(Table 5, p5).

Integrator-owned circuitry (Table 1, p3; Table 2, p4): BOOT to SW capacitor (100 nF typ);
VCC ceramic capacitor >= 1 uF to GND; input capacitor (10 uF typ); inductor (33 uH in
Table 2); output capacitor (22 uF in Table 2).

Design equations a board must satisfy (section 8.4, p26-28):
- Eq. 35: CIN,min = IOUT / (4 * VPP,max * fSW); VPP typically 5 % of VIN,max.
- Eq. 36: dIL = (VIN - VOUT) / L * TON = VOUT / L * TOFF; ripple 20 % to 40 % of IOUT
  (section 8.4.2); Eq. 37: Lmin = VOUT / dIL,max * (1 - Dmin) / fSW.
- Eq. 38: 0.4 <= QP <= 1.33 (QP from Eq. 13, section 7.1) bounds the inductor value for the
  internal slope compensation.
- Eq. 39: IL,PK = IOUT + dIL / 2 must stay below the current limit (Table 6).
- Eq. 42: COUT,BW,min = 4.02 / ((fSW / 10) * VOUT) = 30.5 uF at 400 kHz and 3.3 V.
- Eq. 43: COUT,BW,max = 0.48e-3 / VOUT = 145 uF at 3.3 V: the largest output capacitance
  the internal compensation network supports.
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Voltage")

Mpn = enum("L6981N33DR", "L6981C33DR")
mpn = config(Mpn, default="L6981N33DR", help="Fitted variant: N = low-noise (LNM), C = low-consumption (LCM)")

# Table 6, p6-7: VIN operating range, fixed 3.3 V output (TJ -40 to 125 C), VCC LDO output.
VIN = io(Power(voltage="3.5V to 38V"))
VOUT = io(Power(voltage="3.284V to 3.346V"))
VCC = io(Power(voltage="3.0V to 3.6V"))
GND = io(Ground)
EN = io(Net)
SW = io(Net)
BOOT = io(Net)

Component(
    name="L6981",
    prefix="IC",
    symbol=Symbol(library="L6981.kicad_sym", name=mpn.value),
    footprint=File("SOIC127P600X175-8N.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn=mpn.value, manufacturer="STMicroelectronics"),
    pins={
        "SW": SW,
        "BOOT": BOOT,
        "VCC": VCC,
        "VOUT/FB": VOUT,
        "EN/CLKIN": EN,
        "AGND": GND,
        "VIN": VIN,
        "PGND": GND,
    },
)
